From 9d8a41e5b2f282accab3180626cbc6a27d491883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZonicExists <71136987+zonicisalive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:22:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 24/42] bitproxy: trusted Wi-Fi networks go Direct

List of Wi-Fi names (typed or 'Add current Wi-Fi') where every app goes
Direct and DNS resolves locally; blocked apps stay blocked. Implemented
as sing-box wifi_ssid rules, so joining or leaving a network needs no
reload. Android only reveals SSIDs with location permission ('Allow all
the time' for the service); the card requests it, and Apply refuses
while it is missing, because upstream would otherwise refuse to start
the VPN.
